INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal='Identify top-3 single-month volume anomalies in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by region×product_line, report their multiples vs 24-month mean with return rates, assess real demand vs channel stuffing, and produce a saved Markdown report with source annotations and charts.'):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), unique regions, unique product lines, and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute 24-month rolling mean & anomaly multiples: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month trailing mean of monthly sales volume, then compute the ratio = current_month_sales / 24-month_mean for every month. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/anomaly_ratios.csv) with columns: region, product_line, month, sales_volume, mean_24m, ratio → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the anomaly_ratios.csv, select the top 3 (region, product_line, month) by ratio. For each, look up the return_rate (or equivalent column) for that exact month from the original CSV. Save a small summary CSV (offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv) with columns: rank, region, product_line, month, sales_volume, mean_24m, ratio, return_rate → code_agent
4. Assess real demand vs channel stuffing: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute supporting signals from the CSV: (a) return_rate for the anomaly month vs the 24-month average return_rate for that region×product_line; (b) whether the following 1-3 months show a sharp drop (reversion); (c) whether the spike is isolated or part of a trend. Save a signals CSV (offline_data/stuffing_signals.csv) → code_agent
5. Generate charts: Create 2-3 charts as PNG files: (1) bar chart of top-3 anomaly ratios; (2) line chart showing the 24-month sales trend for each top-3 combination highlighting the anomaly month; (3) return-rate comparison bar chart. Save to offline_data/charts/ → code_agent
6. Write Markdown report: Write a comprehensive Markdown report (offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md) with: H1 title, data tables for top-3 anomalies and signals, embedded chart images, every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）', and a concluding paragraph judging real demand vs channel stuffing for each anomaly. All data from local CSV only. → code_agent
